--- body ---
## Context

Split from ticket 0693 by the raid's Imagine phase (2026-09-06). This is
**not** a direct author request: neither ticket 0686 nor the author's
2026-09-06 remarks ask for a notification channel. It is motivated by
ecosystem convention -- most widely-adopted Zotero plugins surface
background-task feedback through a transient, non-blocking toast rather
than requiring the user to keep a dialog open. That argument holds up, but
it is this ticket's own synthesis, not a ratified decision, and it adds
new accessibility surface (screen-reader announcement of transient toasts,
timing, dismissal) on top of ticket 0686's already-open, still-unverified
accessibility items. Get a quick author nod before building this -- it is
cheap to ask and the alternative is stacking unverified a11y surface on
unverified a11y surface.

## Mechanism

Use **`Zotero.ProgressWindow`** (Zotero's own bundled global) directly,
not `zotero-plugin-toolkit`. This plugin has zero build tooling -- no
`package.json`, no bundler; `bootstrap.js`/`scheduler.js` load raw via
`Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript`. Pulling in `zotero-plugin-toolkit`
would mean introducing a bundler for the first time solely to get a toast.
`Zotero.ProgressWindow` needs no new dependency and no build step, and is
the same primitive the toolkit wraps.

## Design

Add toasts for: job start ("Indexing: <title>", per 0691's vocabulary),
job completion, and a terminal failure (one that will not be retried) --
not on every progress tick, and not once per document in an overnight
sweep of many documents (that would mean dozens of toasts per run, which
cuts against the sitter's "supervise quietly" design). Pin down before
writing acceptance tests: does "job completion" mean per-document or
per-sweep? Default to per-sweep (one completion toast when the whole
overnight run finishes, or goes idle) unless the author says otherwise --
per-document toasts do not match unattended overnight operation.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Toasts use `Zotero.ProgressWindow`; no new dependency added.
- [x] Author has confirmed this ticket should proceed (recorded in the log).
- [ ] Toast cadence is per-sweep, not per-document, unless the author's
      answer says otherwise.
- [ ] Toast text uses only the vocabulary from ticket 0691 -- no internal
      jargon.
